    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Fish moved to recommit to Judiciary.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H34400",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "17:53:30",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House adopted the amendment as agreed to by the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H35000",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "17:53:03",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32600",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "17:52:08",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House rose from the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union to report H.R. 1236.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "15:32:34",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Douglas suggested the absence of a quorum and a quorum call was ordered. Prior to the Call in Committee, the Chair announced that the time for a recorded vote on the pending Douglas amendment, if ordered, would be reduced to five minutes in length.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "14:23:41",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - The Committee of the Whole proceeded with one hour of general debate.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32400",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "14:23:29",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The Speaker designated the Honorable David E. Skaggs to act as Chairman of the Committee.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32020",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "14:23:28",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "House resolved itself into the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union pursuant to H. Res. 373 and Rule XXIII.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "14:23:15",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1236 with 1 hour of general debate. Previous question shall be considered as ordered without intervening motions except motion to recommit. Measure will be read by section. Bill is open to amendments.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "14:23:10",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 373.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L220",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-18",
   "actionTime": "14:22:34",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule H. Res. 373 passed House.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "1990-04-03",
   "actionTime": "13:01:30",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 373 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1236 with 1 hour of general debate. Previous question shall be considered as ordered without intervening motions except motion to recommit. Measure will be read by section. Bill is open to amendments.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
